                    "message": "The macro is from `include/libpldm/firmware_update.h`\nand `pin` is our variable name, we can choose it ourselves.\n\n\n```\n  /**\n   * Declare consumer support for at most revision 1 of the firmware update\n   * package header\n   *\n   * @param name The name for the pin object\n   *\n   * The pin object must be provided to @ref decode_pldm_firmware_update_package\n   */\n  #define DEFINE_PLDM_PACKAGE_FORMAT_PIN_FR01H(name)                             \\\n  |       struct pldm_package_format_pin name = { \\\n  |       |       .meta = { \\\n  |       |       |       .magic = ( \\\n  |       |       |       |       LIBPLDM_SIZEAT(struct pldm_package, iter) + \\\n  |       |       |       |       LIBPLDM_SIZEAT(struct pldm__package_header_information, pac  kage_version_string) + \\\n  |       |       |       |       LIBPLDM_SIZEAT(struct pldm_package_firmware_device_id_recor  d, firmware_device_package_data) + \\\n  |       |       |       |       LIBPLDM_SIZEAT(struct pldm_descriptor, descriptor_data) + \\\n  |       |       |       |       LIBPLDM_SIZEAT(struct pldm_package_component_image_informat  ion, component_version_string) \\\n  |       |       |       ), \\\n  |       |       |       .version = 0u, \\\n  |       |       }, \\\n  |       |       .format = { \\\n  |       |       |       .identifier = PLDM_PACKAGE_HEADER_IDENTIFIER_V1_0, \\\n  |       |       |       .revision = PLDM_PACKAGE_HEADER_FORMAT_REVISION_FR01H, \\\n  |       |       } \\\n  |       }\n```\n\nWe have to define the pin as it gets passed through to libpldm  functions."
                },
                {
                    "file": "common/pldm/pldm_package_util.cpp",
                    "line": 42,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "nit: drop we"
                },
                {
                    "file": "common/pldm/pldm_package_util.cpp",
                    "line": 42,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "common/pldm/pldm_package_util.cpp",
                    "line": 45,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "I am wondering if this has to be a shared_ptr? Isn't the caller suppose to extract the image out and then just let it go?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "common/pldm/pldm_package_util.cpp",
                    "line": 45,
                    "reviewer": {
